# Carbonara

## Ingredients

- Pasta: 12 oz (340g) spaghetti or bucatini.
- Pork: 4 oz (113g) guanciale (cured pork jowl) or pancetta, diced.
- Cheese: 1 cup freshly grated Pecorino Romano (or a mix of Pecorino and Parmigiano-Reggiano).
- Eggs: 2 whole large eggs and 2 large egg yolks.
- Seasoning: Lots of freshly cracked black pepper and salt for the pasta water
- Ingredient 2


## Instructions

- Boil the Pasta: Bring a large pot of water to a boil and season it generously with salt. Cook the pasta until it is al dente (firm to the bite).
- Render the Pork: While the pasta cooks, heat a large skillet over medium heat. Add the guanciale or pancetta and cook until the fat has rendered and the meat is golden and crispy.
- Whisk the Sauce Base: In a medium bowl, whisk together the eggs, egg yolks, and grated cheese. Add a generous amount of black pepper.
- Reserve Pasta Water: Just before draining, scoop out about 1 cup of the starchy pasta cooking water; this is essential for emulsifying the sauce.
- Combine Pasta and Pork: Use tongs to transfer the hot pasta directly from the water into the skillet with the crispy pork. Toss well to coat the noodles in the rendered fat.
- Emulsify the Sauce: Remove the skillet from the heat to prevent the eggs from scrambling. Pour in the egg and cheese mixture and toss vigorously. Slowly add splashes of the reserved pasta water while continuing to toss until the sauce becomes thick, glossy, and creamy.
